==English==
[[Image:BluegrassBanjo.jpg|thumb|right|upright=0.68|A bluegrass banjo]]
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
From the pronunciation of African slaves, of unknown ultimate origin. Possibly a corruption of {{m|en|bandore}} (from {{der|en|es|bandurria}}), alternatively from a West African language such as {{der|en|mnk|banjul}}, or {{der|en|kmb|mbanza}}.
<ref>{{R:OED2}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|băn'jō|a=UK}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈbæn.dʒəʊ/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbæn.d͡ʒoʊ/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-banjo.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|es}}

# A stringed musical instrument ([[chordophone]]), usually with a round body, a [[membrane]]-like [[soundboard]] and a fretted neck, played by plucking or strumming the strings.
#: {{ux|en|I come from Alabama with my '''banjo''' on my knee...}}
#* {{see citations|en}}
# Any of various similar [[musical instrument]]s, such as the Tuvan [[doshpuluur]], with a membrane-like soundboard.
# {{lb|en|slang}} An object shaped like a banjo, especially a [[frying pan]] or a [[shovel]].
# {{lb|en|UK|Dagenham}} A [[cul-de-sac]] with a round end.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1963|author=Peter Willmott|title=The Evolution of a Community|page=75
|passage=They all came back here — we cleared the room and put up tables for the reception — and then we went to another house on the '''banjo''' for a "knees-up".}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=M. C. Dutton|title=The Godfathers of London
|passage=Billy Tower lived in the far left house in the '''banjo''' that was Dagenham's version of cul de sacs. The trouble was you could be seen from the house and, in the time it took to walk along the Banjo, drugs could be flushed away.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=Martin Crookston|title=Garden Suburbs of Tomorrow?|passage=The '''banjo''' format is not an unalloyed success these days: kids playing noisily on the quite narrow common green {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|mining}} A miner's round-nosed shovel.
# {{lb|en|Malaysia}} An [[egg sandwich]] fried on a [[flattop]] and served in a [[bun]] like a burger, {{ellipsis of|en|egg banjo|nocap=1}}.
# {{lb|en|slang|vulgar}} The [[frenulum]] of the [[penis]].

