{{bor+|en|ja|忍者|tr=ninja}}, of uncertain derivation but with an underlying sense of secret or hidden person. Popularized in Japanese by [[manga]] after [[World War II]] and in English by the 1980 novel {{w|The Ninja (novel)|The Ninja}} by {{w|Eric Van Lustbader}} and the 1981 movie ''{{w|Enter the Ninja}}''

{{sno|en|Mongolian miner|t=Mongolian miner|cap=1}} arose from the supposed resemblance of the bowls used to wash [[ore]] with [[mercury]] to the shells of the main characters from ''{{w|Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles}}''.

The [[Juggalo]] slang sense arose via influence from [[AAVE]] {{m|en|nigga}}.

