===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|pt|baniano}}, from {{der|en|ar|بَنِيَان}}, from {{der|en|gu|વાણિયો||merchant}}, from {{der|en|sa|वाणिज|tr=vāṇijá}}, from earlier {{m|sa|वणिज्|tr=vaṇíj||merchant, trader}}. The name appears to have been first bestowed popularly on a famous tree of this species growing near [[w:Bandar Abbas|Bandar Abbas]], under which the ''[[Bannian]]s'', or Hindu traders settled at that port, had built a little pagoda.<ref>{{cite-book|url=http://dsal.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/philologic/getobject.pl?c.0:1:145.hobson|author=Yule, Henry, Sir. Hobson-Jobson|title=A glossary of colloquial Anglo-Indian words and phrases, and of kindred terms, etymological, historical, geographical and discursive.|location=London|publisher=J. Murray|year=1903}}</ref> {{doublet|en|bunnia}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbæn.jæn/|/ˈbæn.jən/|a=UK,US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-banyan.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ænjən|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ban|yan}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An Indian [[trader]], [[merchant]], [[cashier]], or [[money changer]].
# A [[tropical]] [[Indian]] [[fig]] [[tree]], {{taxfmt|Ficus benghalensis|species}}, that has many [[aerial root]]s.
#: {{syn|en|banyan tree}}
#* {{RQ:Smile Investigations|chapter=[Letter dated March 18th, 1878]|page=4|passage=When doubling a point, which was covered with a heavy growth of the '''banian''' mangrove, which extended into deep water, we discovered a party of Kubu Orangs fishing from off a pack of drift that had lodged against the inward trend of the northern shore.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The East I Know|page=33|pageurl=http://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015011885913;seq=53;num=33|author=Teresa Frances; William Rose Benét|by=w:Paul Claudel|year=1914|passage=We climb and then descend; we pass by the great '''banyan''' which, like Atlas, settling himself powerfully on his contorted haunches, seems awaiting with knee and shoulder the burden of the sky.}}
# Various other trees of the {{taxfmt|Ficus|genus}} subgenus {{taxlink|Urostigma|subgenus}}, especially {{taxlink|Ficus pertusa|species}} ({{vern|Central American banyan}}) and {{taxlink|Ficus microcarpa|species}} ({{vern|Chinese banyan}} or {{vern|Malayan banyan}}).
# A type of loose [[gown]] worn in India.
# {{lb|en|India|Pakistan}} A [[vest]]; an [[undershirt]]; a [[singlet]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1889|year_published=1899|author={{w|Rudyard Kipling}}|title={{w|Under the Deodars}}|chapter=At the Pit's Mouth|location=Boston|publisher=The Greenock Press|page=50|text=It was an honest letter, written by an honest man, then stewing in the Plains on two hundred rupees a month (for he allowed his wife eight hundred and fifty), and in a silk '''banian''' and cotton trousers.}}
# {{lb|en|British|naval|_|slang|dated}} A camping [[excursion]] on shore, to give a ship's [[crew]] a break from [[shipboard]] [[routine]].

