===Etymology===
{{swp|Britain (name)}}
{{swp|la:[[+ (discretiva)|+]]}}
{{etymon|la|id=Britain|:bor|grc:Βρεττανία<id:Britain>}}
Attested from the 1st century {{BCE}}, directly or from {{bor|la|grc|Βρεττανία}}, {{m|grc|Πρεττανία}} (in {{w|Diodorus}}), earlier {{m|grc|[[νῆσος]] [[Πρεττανική]]}} or {{m|grc|Βρεττανίαι}}, used by {{w|Pytheas}} (4th century {{BCE}}) of the entire archipelago now known as the [[British Isles]].

The Ancient Greek name is ultimately from a {{der|la|cel|-}} ethnonym, reconstructed as early {{der|la|cel-bry|-}} {{m|cel-pro|*Pritani}}, perhaps from a {{der|la|cel-pro|*Kʷritanī}}, {{m|cel-pro|*Kʷritenī}}, whence {{cog|cy|Prydyn||Picts}}, {{cog|mga|Cruithne}}, {{m|mga|Cruithentúaith|Cruithen-túaith|Picts}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*kʷer-||to do}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA}}
* Note: only found in hexameters with a short first syllable, except for a single instance of /britt-/ in Lucretius. [[w:ca:Sergi_(gramàtic)|Sergius]] on Donatus testifies to /a:n/ rather than /ann/. Romance descendants seem to consistently point to /tt/.

===Proper noun===
{{la-proper noun|Britannia<1.both>}}

# {{place|la|t=Britain|region|r/Western Europe|the country of the [[Briton]]s}}
